Package: esidx
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34)
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: ext4 search index engine with an Everything (ETP) server
 esidx walks a directory tree into a snapshot, answers Everything's search language
 (ext:, dc:, dm:, size:, parent:, path:, wildcards, boolean and grouping) over the ETP
 protocol, and reconciles that snapshot from kernel filesystem events so it stays current
 without a periodic rescan.
 .
 The event source is fanotify, which needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN. In this deployment one process
 holds it: the unit starts esidx as root, the binary opens the fanotify group, gives the
 capability back before it opens the listener, and keeps only CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH -- the
 one thing that turns an event into a path. What the process is allowed to hold is stated
 in the unit's CapabilityBoundingSet, so the ceiling is a property of the install rather
 than a promise in a comment.
 .
 The two-process form is still shipped: sfa-server is installed as well, a root proxy that
 hands absolute paths over a group-owned socket to an unprivileged esidx. Upgrading from a
 package that ran it retires the two units it used.
 .
 This package installs one systemd unit, esidx.service, and the configuration it reads
 (/etc/default/esidx). It enables the unit but does not start it: the server needs a
 snapshot, and building the first one scans the tree, which does not belong in a
 maintainer script. The install output says the two commands.
